  "question": "A die is rolled. Consider events: $A=\\{1, 2, 5\\}, B=\\{3, 5\\}, C=\\{2, 3, 4, 5\\}$ and hence find:<br />**(i)** $P(A|C)$ and $P(C|A)$<br />**(ii)** $P(A \\cap B|C)$ and $P(A \\cup B|C)$",
  "answeroption": "",
  "explanation": "**(i)** **Step 1:** $A \\cap C = \\{2, 5\\}$. $P(A \\cap C) = 2/6$, $P(C) = 4/6$, $P(A) = 3/6$.<br />**Step 2:** $P(A|C) = P(A \\cap C)/P(C) = (2/6)/(4/6) = 1/2$.<br />**Step 3:** $P(C|A) = P(A \\cap C)/P(A) = (2/6)/(3/6) = 2/3$.<br /><br />**(ii)** **Step 1:** $A \\cap B = \\{5\\}$. $(A \\cap B) \\cap C = \\{5\\}$. $P((A \\cap B) \\cap C) = 1/6$.<br />**Step 2:** $P(A \\cap B|C) = P((A \\cap B) \\cap C)/P(C) = (1/6)/(4/6) = 1/4$.<br />**Step 3:** $A \\cup B = \\{1, 2, 3, 5\\}$. $(A \\cup B) \\cap C = \\{2, 3, 5\\}$. $P((A \\cup B) \\cap C) = 3/6$.<br />**Step 4:** $P(A \\cup B|C) = P((A \\cup B) \\cap C)/P(C) = (3/6)/(4/6) = 3/4$.",
